The In Memoriam stanza (abba
                           4
                           )  is named after Tennyson's poem (though that was by no means its first use), because Tennyson gave it a peculiar melody, and, partly for this reason and partly from the length and subject of the poem, almost preëmpted it for elegiac purposes.[53]  Characteristic stanzas metrically are these:
